                    576.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "If your need for leave is foreseeable, you must give the Company at least 30 days prior notice of the need for leave, preferably written. If this is not possible, you must at least give notice as soon as practicable (generally within one to two business days of learning of your need for leave). Failure to provide such notice may be grounds for delay of leave. Additionally, if you are planning a medical treatment, you must consult with the Company first regarding the dates of such treatment. Where the need for leave is not foreseeable, you should notify the Company as soon as possible and practical.",
            "block_bbox": [
                341,
                602,
                1462,
                777
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
